This product includes software adapted from the following Apache-2.0 projects:

- NVIDIA-NeMo/Evaluator (https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Evaluator)
  Portions of the native evaluation kernel (scorer library, evaluation loop,
  dataset URI loading, and sandbox handling under aqa/eval/) are adapted from
  NeMo Evaluator, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

- EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness (https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness)
  Used as an optional evaluation harness via the `lm_eval` adapter.

- TencentQQGYLab/ELLA (https://github.com/TencentQQGYLab/ELLA)
  DPG-Bench: the benchmark metadata (recipes/data/dpgbench/dpg_bench.csv) is
  vendored verbatim, and aqa/eval/dpgbench.py ports
  dpg_bench/compute_dpg_bench.py (VQA-judged per-proposition scoring with
  dependency zeroing and category aggregation).

- tyxsspa/AnyText (https://github.com/tyxsspa/AnyText)
  The Acc/NED text-rendering scoring semantics in aqa/eval/glyphdraw2.py are
  adapted from eval/eval_dgocr.py (per-line exact-match accuracy and the
  normalized character edit distance).  GlyphDraw2 ships no runnable scorer, so
  this public evaluator defines the metric.

- PKU-YuanGroup/WISE (https://github.com/PKU-YuanGroup/WISE)
  WISE_Verified: the prompts (recipes/data/wise/) are vendored and
  aqa/eval/wise.py ports the binary judge instruction, score extraction and
  category-weighted aggregation from vllm_eval.py + calculate_verified.py.
  (The repository declares no license file; the paper is arXiv:2503.07265.)

This product also includes software adapted from the following MIT projects:

- djghosh13/geneval (https://github.com/djghosh13/geneval)
  Copyright (c) 2023 Dhruba Ghosh. The GenEval prompt set + COCO class list
  (recipes/data/geneval/) are vendored verbatim, and the detection-based
  scoring logic in aqa/eval/geneval.py is a port of
  evaluation/evaluate_images.py + summary_scores.py (with the detector swapped
  from mmdet's Mask2Former to transformers' Mask2FormerForUniversalSegmentation).

- OPPO-Mente-Lab/GlyphDraw2 (https://github.com/OPPO-Mente-Lab/GlyphDraw2)
  The prompt files (recipes/data/glyphdraw2/) are vendored verbatim.

Additionally, the CVTG-2K prompts (recipes/data/cvtg2k/) are vendored from the
HuggingFace dataset dnkdnk/CVTG-2K (https://huggingface.co/datasets/dnkdnk/CVTG-2K,
Apache License 2.0), and aqa/eval/cvtg2k.py ports the Word Accuracy / NED /
CLIPScore computation from NJU-PCALab/TextCrafter's
TextCrafter_Eval/unified_metrics_eval.py (arXiv:2503.23461; the repository
declares no license file).

Each adapted file retains an attribution header pointing to its upstream source.
